{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>As much as they can carry.</b> The Ramban, of blessed memory, explained: more than what their money that they brought him would warrant." "<b>And put each man's silver in the mouth of his sack.</b> This silver was with their knowledge. For had he done this as the first time — without their knowledge — they would have had a defense regarding the goblet, which was treated just as the silver was treated. But this was with their knowledge, and they recognized the silver just as they recognized the grain, for they recognized that he had given them 'as much as they can carry.' And had it been without their knowledge, perhaps he could have claimed against them that the silver this time too was hidden away — but such is not plausible regarding the goblet. And who can contend with one mightier than himself?" "<b>And know</b> that because the provisioners were very numerous throughout the land of Egypt, and there was much turmoil within it, those who came would give their sacks and their silver to the provisioner, and he would measure out to them according to the silver found, and they would take what was given them, since 'the king's word rules' — and besides, he deals in faithfulness. Therefore they took, both the first time and the second time, their sacks sealed and did not know what was inside them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:06.692910411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}